Four entries in the book's tables are cut off (truncated) instead of rounded:
\(e^{3} = 20.0855\ldots \approx 20.086\) (printed 20.085);
\(e^{10} = 22026.4658\ldots \approx 22026.466\) (printed 22026.465);
\(e^{-1} = 0.36788\ldots \approx 0.368\) (printed 0.367);
\(e^{-3} = 0.049787\ldots \approx 0.0498\) (printed 0.0497).
The book's own Figure 1.6 uses the rounded value \((-1, 0.37)\).
